@@@!atrep-exo
@=kolophon=>tei

@@/ TEI export of a colophon: the fields a publicationStmt has an
@@/ element for as that element (publisher, pubPlace, date), any
@@/ other field an idno typed with the field name - the one
@@/ element of the statement that takes a free type. The
@@/ normalized value of the date (the chronos aphanes) is the
@@/ date's when-iso: the attribute takes every ISO 8601 form a
@@/ chronos does, an interval included, where when takes a
@@/ single date. The enclosing publicationStmt is written by
@@/ the host exo, which places the block in the header.

@%
& &amp;
< &lt;
> &gt;
" &quot;
%@

@-> *paragraph
@(grammata)
>-@

@-> :(officina)
<publisher>@(grammata)</publisher>
>-@

@-> :(locus)
<pubPlace>@(grammata)</pubPlace>
>-@

@-> :(datum)
<date@[ when-iso="@(chronos)"]@>@(grammata)</date>
>-@

@-> :
<idno type="@(lemma)">@(grammata)</idno>
>-@
